      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name was changed to Hampton in 1909, reflecting its growing identity beyond just a railroad junction.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hampton%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1931, Hampton annexed land from Glen Gardner and Bethlehem Township, resolving a long-standing border dispute.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
